# Data persistence documentation

[`docs/architecture/data-persistence.md`](docs/architecture/data-persistence.md) is the architecture SoT for **stores, record shapes, relations, and access flows**. It is not a backlog — phased work stays in [`docs/plans/`](docs/plans/).

## Keep the doc in sync

When you **add, remove, or change** a durable store, schema, relation, or how records are read/written, update `docs/architecture/data-persistence.md` **in the same PR**. Bump **Last updated**. Refresh mermaid diagrams that the change invalidates. Do not leave the doc describing a store or field that no longer exists.

| Change | Update in the persistence doc |
|--------|-------------------------------|
| New Table / collection / Stripe object / vault secret that holds records or config the app reads | Systems of record table + the matching section + source map |
| Contact / profile columns, personas, related-contact rules, People partition | §1 entity tables and relations ER |
| Permission IDs, roles, or how `permissionGate` authorizes People | §1.2 catalog + People sequence |
| Content Zod / Astro collection / site-settings / resume-meta fields | §2 models and git ER |
| Publish mode, commit paths, or media write location | §2.4 publish sequence |
| Lesson rates ↔ Stripe `lesson_rate_id`, Payment Links, webhook persistence | §3 Stripe + pay sequence |
| Inquiry (or any public form) starts or stops writing a store | §5 transient vs SoT; move to a store section if it persists |
| New store (Postgres, Calendar, LTV match, inquiry → CRM) | Systems of record + new section; remove it from “not persisted yet” |
| Drop a store or make a path notify-only again | Delete or mark transient; do not leave stale SoT rows |

Also add the new source file to this rule’s `globs` when you introduce a store module that is not already listed.

## What does not need a doc edit

Comment-only or typo fixes in the globbed files. Adding a markdown **content** file that already matches an existing collection schema (`src/content/shows/*.md`, and so on). Secret **value** rotation with no new secret **name**.

